The export GITHUB_TOKEN="your_github_personal_access_token_here" command is used in your terminal (Linux/macOS) to store your GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT) as an environment variable. This allows Git operations, GitHub CLI (gh), or other automation tools to securely authenticate without requiring a username and password.To use this properly, you will need to replace "your_github_personal_access_token_here" with your actual, private token.How to Generate Your TokenIf you do not have a token yet, you can create one by navigating to your GitHub Personal Access Tokens Page and following these steps:Click Generate new token.Choose between Fine-grained tokens (recommended) or Tokens (classic).Select the scopes/permissions your project needs (e.g., repo, workflow, or admin:org).Click Generate token.Copy the token immediately, as GitHub will not display it again.How to Apply the CommandOpen your terminal and execute the following, substituting your actual token:bashexport GITHUB_TOKEN="github_pat_YourActualTokenHere"
Use code with caution.Making the Variable PermanentThis command only lasts for your current terminal session. If you close the terminal, the token will be lost. To make it permanent across all future sessions:On Linux / macOS: Run echo 'export GITHUB_TOKEN="github_pat_YourActualTokenHere"' >> ~/.bashrc (or ~/.zshrc if you are using Zsh), and then run source ~/.bashrc.On Windows (PowerShell): Run [System.Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable("GITHUB_TOKEN", "github_pat_YourActualTokenHere", "User").If you tell me what specific tool or project you are trying to authenticate (e.g., the GitHub CLI, a CI/CD pipeline, or a Git client), I can give you the exact steps to use this token for that workflow.3 sitesManaging your personal access tokens - GitHub DocsVerify your email address, if it hasn't been verified yet. In the upper-right corner of any page on GitHub, click your profile pic...docs.github.comQuick Start - DevStream - Your DevOps Toolchain Manager13 Dec 2022 — Bash ./dtm show config -t quickstart > config.yaml. Then set the following environment variables by running (replace values within...docs.devstream.ioGitHub Access Tokens: How To Use Them Properly17 Jan 2024 — what is going on guys welcome back in this video today we're going to learn how to properly use personal access tokens when authen...7:33YouTube·NeuralNineShow all   
